From e56ef83b59b621575bfbfec580eafae3cfb1d2ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 05:36:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] h2: client: carry the no-follow-redirect preference onto
 stream 1

When a client connection negotiates h2 via ALPN, the original request is
migrated onto a new stream wsi (sid 1).  The migration copied wsi->flags but
not client_no_follow_redirect, which lives in its own bitfield, so the first
request on every fresh h2 connection followed redirects even when the caller
connected with LCCSCF_HTTP_NO_FOLLOW_REDIRECT.  Requests adopted onto an
existing h2 connection keep their own wsi and were not affected.

Copy the bit across with the rest of the client state.

Backport of the lib/roles/h2/http2.c hunk of upstream
e56ef83b59b621575bfbfec580eafae3cfb1d2ef (main, "interceptor: clean up bot
warnings"), adapted to v5.0-stable ac23cae70.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/roles/h2/http2.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/roles/h2/http2.c b/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
index 775a8fc75..ae543b08f 100644
--- a/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
+++ b/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
@@ -1745,6 +1745,14 @@ lws_h2_parse_end_of_frame(struct lws *wsi)
 #endif
 #if defined(LWS_WITH_CLIENT)
 			h2n->swsi->flags = wsi->flags;
+			/*
+			 * The no-follow preference lives in its own bitfield,
+			 * it has to be brought over separately or the first
+			 * stream on the connection follows redirects the user
+			 * code asked not to follow
+			 */
+			h2n->swsi->client_no_follow_redirect =
+					wsi->client_no_follow_redirect;
 #if defined(LWS_WITH_CONMON)
 			/* sid1 needs to represent the connection experience
 			 * ... we take over responsibility for the DNS list
